# `while (i < j) { swap(list, i, j); i++; j--; while (list[i] < t) i++; while (list[j] > t) j--; }`: the partition of a quickselect. `i` and `j` enter as numbers of which nothing says that they are whole.
# A counter is asked for an int32 in front of its loop where every way round brings a step of it. The parameter of the head of a loop INSIDE joins a name of the counter, from outside that loop, with its own step,
# which is no name yet when the parameter is met: so a counter that a loop inside steps too was "not stepped all round", both went round as doubles, and every read and store under them went by the generic road.
# Now such a parameter is taken on trust where every way from outside its loop brings a name, and at the end every way into it must have brought one (part).
# Not where the head inside holds the parameter against a bound, `for (; i < stop; i++)`: that loop is bought for itself, with its counter, its bound and the room of its views asked in front of IT (bounded).
# Where the trust fails, `k = i; while (list[k] > k) k = list[k]`, the answer is the one of before: `i` stays the counter that it was (strays).
